        "date": "2026-11-24T21:01:01Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): set a tool's holder and stick-out in the tool library window\n\nThe Tool tab of the tool library window gets an assembly group: the\nholder pick, the gauge length, the projection (stick-out), their total,\nthe shank warning, a taper that is not the machine's spindle mount, and\nthe refusal of Apply holder before the click. Apply holder is the one\nundoable SetToolBody::library. The window keeps its own holder draft.\nA change of the stored tool's length re-seeds only the projection draft\n(#808 item 2). The preview draws the draft holder.\n\nRefs #808\nFixes #3895\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
